      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a ticket classifier.\n\nGiven this ticket:\nCustomer: {{ $('Google Sheets Trigger').item.json['Customer Name'] }}\nEmail: {{ $('Google Sheets Trigger').item.json['Email'] }}\nTicket: {{ $('Google Sheets Trigger').item.json['Ticket Text'] }}\n\nDo the following:\n1. Copy customer_name, customer_email, and ticket_text exactly as given above, with no changes.\n2. Classify category: Billing, Technical, Account, or General\n3. Classify urgency using these strict rules:\n   - High: the ticket mentions any of these specifically — the service/app/platform being \"down,\" an \"outage,\" complete inability to access the service, data loss, a security breach, or explicitly states they are losing customers/money/business RIGHT NOW because of this issue.\n   - Low: everything else, including billing questions, refund requests, single bugs or crashes affecting only the customer themselves, login resets, how-to questions, and general account changes.\n   \n   If the ticket contains the words \"down,\" \"outage,\" or says the business is losing customers/revenue because of the issue, you MUST classify it as High. Do not classify these as Low under any circumstance.\n   \n   Default to Low only when none of the above High triggers are present.\nOutput only customer_name, customer_email, ticket_text, category, and urgency.",
